<title>UK: Metals ship in Red Sea to be refloated from Feb 12.</title>
<headline>Metals ship in Red Sea to be refloated from Feb 12.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Attempts to refloat the Chinese-flag vessel Zi Yun Shan, aground in the Rea Sea, are to be made after February 12 when its cargo has been shifted and repairs made, Lloyds Shipping Intelligence Service said on Monday.</p>
<p>The 33,663-dwt vessel, with a cargo of 24,000 tonnes of mainly bulk/bagged aluminium, bauxite and barite, ran aground some 20 days ago on the south west rocks at lat 13 38.15n, long 42 35.9e., Lloyds added.</p>
</text>
